gth = 0\\n           max_substring = ""\\n           while start < len(s):\\n             for char in s[start:]:\\n               if s[start:start + len(char)] not in s[:start]:\\n                 if len(char) > max_length:\\n                   max_length = len(char)\\n                   max_substring = char\\n             start += 1\\n           return max_substring\\n         ```\\n         Can you optimize the function to have a time complexity of O(N) and explain the optimization?\\n       """,\n       "difficulty": "hard",\n       "follow_up": "Can you also discuss the trade-offs between using a sliding window approach versus a brute-force approach?"\n     },\n     {\n       "topic": "SQLAlchemy",\n       "question": """\\n         Write a SQLAlchemy query that retrieves a user\'s information from the database. However, the current implementation has a bug that leads to a database deadlock.\\n         ```python\\n         from sqlalchemy import select\\n\\n         db = SessionLocal()\\n         user = db.query(User).join(User.orders).first()\\n         order = user.orders[0]\\n         db.query(Order).filter(Order.id == order.id).update({"status": "shipped"})\\n         db.commit()\\n         ```\\n         Can you identify the bug and explain how to fix it to avoid the database deadlock?\\n       """,\n       "difficulty": "easy",\n       "follow_up": "Can you also explain why database deadlocks occur and how to prevent them?"\n     },\n     {\n       "topic": "FastAPI",\n       "question": """\\n         Write a FastAPI endpoint that handles POST requests to create a new user. However, the current implementation has a bug that leads to a data inconsistency issue.\\n         ```python\\n         from fastapi import FastAPI, Depends\\n         from sqlalchemy import create_engine\\n         from sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\\n         from pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\n         app = FastAPI()\\n\\n         engine = create_engine(\'postgresql://user:pas